wortnetz is a German version of Zanagrams, an English word game by PZL games
(https://pzlgames.com/games/zanagrams/). It is not connected to PZL games.


The puzzles (puzzles/*.json) and the word lists in gen/ were made with these word data. Their
words, word frequencies (the "z" values) and word forms come from them:

wordfreq
    Robyn Speer and contributors, https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq
    Its word lists are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
    International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/);
    its sources and their credits are listed in wordfreq's README. wortnetz uses the German
    and English frequencies.

igerman98, German dictionary for Hunspell
    Copyright (C) 1999-2016 Björn Jacke, https://www.j3e.de/ispell/igerman98/
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or 3. Used as packaged by
    dictionary-de 3.0.0 (Titus Wormer, https://github.com/wooorm/dictionaries).

Wiktionary, German nouns
    Wiktionary contributors, https://de.wiktionary.org/
    Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0. Used as the noun table of the Python package german-nouns
    1.2.5 (https://github.com/gambolputty/german-nouns), which tells singular nouns from
    plurals for the generator.

The word data themselves are not in this repository; gen/lexicon.py and gen/nouns.py build
what the generator reads from them.


